From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:53:36 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 006/230] Exclude Bot API 8.0 signature field from initData
 check string
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Current Telegram clients attach an Ed25519 signature to every initData
payload. Folding it into the bot-token HMAC check string (the old
exclude-only-hash algorithm) makes every authentic login fail — the
documented Bot API 8.0 algorithm excludes both hash and signature, and
validators that exclude only hash reject authentic payloads.

Excluding it is strictly safe: payloads without the field hash identically
either way. The TEMP probe is replaced by a permanent failure-path ops line
(sent-but-unverified initData = silent Telegram→guest downgrade) and the
verify suite pins the documented algorithm both ways.

